 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p><b>JDBC configuration</b> means setting up everything a Java program needs to connect to a database.</p><h3>Steps</h3><ul><li>Install the database and create the database/table.</li><li>Add the <b>driver JAR</b> (e.g. mysql-connector-j.jar) to the classpath.</li><li>Write the <b>database URL</b>: <code>jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/Shop</code>.</li><li>Load the driver: <code>Class.forName(\"com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver\")</code> (automatic since JDBC 4).</li><li>Connect: <code>DriverManager.getConnection(url, user, password)</code>.</li></ul><table><tr><th>Database</th><th>Driver class</th><th>URL</th></tr><tr><td>MySQL</td><td>com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver</td><td>jdbc:mysql://host:3306/db</td></tr><tr><td>Oracle</td><td>oracle.jdbc.OracleDriver</td><td>jdbc:oracle:thin:@host:1521:xe</td></tr><tr><td>PostgreSQL</td><td>org.postgresql.Driver</td><td>jdbc:postgresql://host:5432/db</td></tr></table>",
 "quiz": {
  "q": "Which part of the URL is the database name in jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/Shop?",
